## Start Flux

In an earlier section, the {{ scheduler_name }} resource manager was installed
and configured for use on both the *head node* and *compute* node instances.
With the cluster nodes up and functional, we can now startup the resource
manager services in preparation for running user jobs. The Flux broker on the
*head node* is rank 0 of the system instance; the brokers on the *compute* nodes
are started on boot and connect to it.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Resource Manager Startup -->
```bash
# Start munge and the Flux system instance on head node
systemctl enable --now munge.service
systemctl enable --now flux.service
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Running systems can pick up most configuration changes with `flux config
reload`, except for changes to the `bootstrap` table, which require restarting
`flux.service` on all nodes.
